      <div type="commentary">
        <p n="1" ana="#tr.layout">Chapter opening: the numeral ⲉ (5) centred with an overline (922–945); the title follows in ll. 2–3. The marginal numerals ⲉ̄ (left 663–687, right 1189–1212) stand between the two title lines (y ≈ 385); they are attached to l. 2.</p>
        <p n="4" ana="#tr.layout">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲡ.</p>
        <p n="7" ana="#tr.layout">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲡ.</p>
        <p n="11" ana="#tr.bracket">The bracket opened before the last three dots is not closed in the edition; it is closed here at the line end. So also ll. 13, 22, 23, 30, 31, 33, 35 and 36; on l. 31 and l. 33 the letters after the bracket (ⲉ ⲡⲛⲁⲃⲉ … ⲧⲉⲧ; ϭ) are part of the restoration.</p>
        <p n="12" ana="#tr.reading">The ϣ of [ⲛ]ϣⲏⲣⲉ has a separate sublinear dot in its lower bowl (7× zoom; the ϣ of ⲛϣⲏⲣⲉ in l. 11 has none); so also ϣ in ll. 23 and 29. The other ϣ on the page carry no dot (6× zoom and blob check).</p>
        <p n="15" ana="#tr.layout">A wide blank, not marked by the editors, stands before the enlarged ⲡ of ⲡⲙⲁϩⲥⲛⲉⲩ.</p>
        <p n="16" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ϩⲛ (967–987, pixel row): ϩ 55 %, ⲛ 60 %, encoded on both.</p>
        <p n="17" ana="#tr.print">The stroke over ⲥ of ⲉⲧⲁϥⲟⲩⲁⲛϩⲥ is printed obliquely. Bars at x 963–975 and 1062–1076 are the descenders of ϩ in l. 16, not strokes.</p>
        <p n="18" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ϥ of ⲧⲏⲣϥ (741–751) and over ⲛ of ⲉⲧϩⲛ (964–976); the bar at 925–937 is a descender from l. 17.</p>
        <p n="22" ana="#tr.bracket">The edition prints a closing bracket after the five dots with no opening bracket on this line or at the end of l. 21; the five dots are encoded as illegible and the bracket as unpaired.</p>
        <p n="24" ana="#tr.source">The whole line is a statement of the editors that it is completely destroyed; encoded with the vocabulary id for destruction, since the intensified wording is not yet in the vocabulary (ledger §2).</p>
        <p n="26" ana="#tr.layout">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲡ. Measured overline over ⲓⲏ[ⲥ] (880–925) covers ⲓ, ⲏ and the restored ⲥ (90 %). Measured stroke over ⲣ of the restored ⲡⲡⲣⲓ̈ⲉ (987–998).</p>
        <p n="27" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ⲙⲛ (933–954): ⲙ 52 %, ⲛ 57 %, encoded on both. The bars at 602–630 are the descender of ϩ in l. 26.</p>
        <p n="29" ana="#tr.reading">ⲯ (arms curved up) in ⲁⲙⲯⲩⲭⲁⲩⲉ, compared at 6× with ϯ of ⲁⲡϯⲟⲩ (l. 8; straight crossbar); so also ⲙⲯⲩⲭⲁⲩⲉ in ll. 32 and 33. The stroke over ⲥ of ⲛϩⲏⲧⲥ is printed obliquely.</p>
        <p n="33" ana="#tr.print">Bars over ⲛ of ⲡⲉϥϣⲛⲉ (860–873) and over ⲙ of ⲙⲯⲩⲭⲁⲩⲉ (966–980) are descenders from l. 32; no stroke is printed there (4× zoom).</p>
        <p n="34" ana="#tr.layout">An enlarged ⲡ begins the restored [ⲡⲙⲁϩϥⲧⲁⲩ] after the editors' "leer".</p>
